<description>
Overlay the two side-by-side foreground masks and render their union in pink.

Input structure
The input is two equal square panels placed horizontally on a black
background. Each panel contains exactly one non-background foreground color,
and the two panel colors are different. Pink is absent from the input.

Rule
Split the grid at the vertical midpoint. For each position in one panel,
output pink if the corresponding cell is foreground in either input panel;
otherwise output black.

Key insight
The yellow and green cells are aligned masks, not colors to preserve; the
output is the boolean union of the two masks recolored to a single color.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "two side-by-side equal square masks on black background: a yellow mask on the left and a green mask on the right",
  "transform": "overlay the two masks by corresponding positions; output pink where either mask has foreground and black elsewhere",
  "grid_shape": "one-panel canvas, same height and half the input width"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    input: 3x6 (two 3x3 panels side by side) [observed]
    output: 3x3 (single panel)
    background: BLACK
  panels:
    layout: left panel = columns 0-2, right panel = columns 3-5
    left_color: YELLOW (4) [observed]
    right_color: GREEN (3) [observed]
    constraint: left and right foreground colors must differ; PINK (6) absent from input
    fg_cells_per_panel: 2-5
    masks_not_identical: union must differ from each individual mask (not fully overlapping)
  output:
    rule: boolean OR of left and right foreground masks, recolored to PINK (6)
    fg_cells: 4-8 (union of both masks)
    intersection_cells: 0-3 (overlap is allowed but masks must not be identical)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct random (task is simple enough)
  steps:
    1. Create a 3x3 left mask by randomly choosing 2-5 cells to be YELLOW on BLACK.
    2. Create a 3x3 right mask by randomly choosing 2-5 cells to be GREEN on BLACK.
    3. Ensure the two masks are not identical (reject if same positions).
    4. Concatenate left and right panels horizontally to form the 3x6 input.
    5. Output = PINK where either mask has foreground, BLACK otherwise.
```
</generation_spec>
